#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162083 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161896 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/id #uuid "4d5a8f9d-7324-547c-ae5e-b49294debc1b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9472" :question/problem "Consider the curves $C_1$ and $C_2,$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{3},\\,t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 3 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨3{u}^{3},\\,3u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose $\\displaystyle\\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = 3k$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k$\n\n- $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k$" :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Notice that $C_1$ and $C_2$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that $C_1$ and $C_2$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{1}{9}y^3, \\quad 0\\leq y\\leq 3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{-C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds  = \\int_{C_1} f(x,y)\\,\\textrm ds = k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049144}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521927 :question-generator/id #uuid "531dfa9b-fae2-5203-b7d6-0abc0aa20c10" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186162083.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162326 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8de278d-ef94-53b3-a37d-10ade572c491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159159} {:answer/id #uuid "db1ebdeb-d8c2-5ee3-bc75-4945f7199fb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159160} {:answer/id #uuid "feddb339-fa62-5dad-8d5b-8385d20d7d34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159161} {:answer/id #uuid "02c1b5cc-f5dd-5df3-aa07-49600ed22732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159162} {:answer/id #uuid "75d4187a-0ea4-5604-bfd9-c405fec10a64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159163}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4f88280b-5b73-509d-b173-5a9d26ec9781" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159158}] :question/id #uuid "03eb9f6c-5710-543d-af91-9b267957eccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-122478" :question/problem "Suppose $\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = 2$ for some function $f(x, y)$, where $C_{1}$ is parametrized by $r_{1}(t) = ⟨t, t^{2}⟩$ for $0 \\le t \\le 1$.\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\n1. $\\displaystyle \\int_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)ds =-2$\n2. $\\displaystyle \\int_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = 2$\n3. $\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{2}}f(x, y)ds = 4$, where $C_{2}$ is parametrized by $r_{2}(u) = ⟨2u, 4u^{2}⟩$ for $0 \\le u \\le \\frac{1}{2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95ed31a0-aafb-51f7-ab3d-e8ff5050b401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159183} {:answer/id #uuid "9e77d5a5-ebf9-5dce-9e8c-ff031c4ef20a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159184} {:answer/id #uuid "a966c171-289b-5056-80b1-a3a81a3dff1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159185} {:answer/id #uuid "1ee86563-d77d-5365-bfcf-19085bedd792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159186} {:answer/id #uuid "299d46ee-11e3-5c2a-8729-11f0f4e10517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159187}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc74610-e88e-565b-911f-e91506b49f46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159182}] :question/id #uuid "c6541032-7a7a-5a1c-bb3c-d0a7d3bd3d1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122571" :question/problem "Consider the curves $C_{1}$ and $C_{2}$, defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}C_{1}:r_{1}(t)|= ⟨\\sin t, \\cos t⟩, & 0 \\le t \\le 2π \\\\ C_{2}:r_{2}(θ)|= ⟨\\sin 2θ, \\cos 2θ⟩, & 0 \\le θ \\le π\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nNow suppose $\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = k$ for some function $f(x, y)$ and real number $k$. Which of the following must be true?\n\n1. $\\displaystyle \\int_{-C_{1}}f(x, y)ds = k$\n2. $\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{2}}f(x, y)ds = k$\n3. $\\displaystyle \\int_{C_{2}}f(x, y)ds = \\frac{1}{2}k$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b877064-2518-5f0a-b4cc-e8ce3cdb6339" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462061} {:answer/id #uuid "d31ab5cc-8f03-565c-baa7-182f415d2e40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b877064-2518-5f0a-b4cc-e8ce3cdb6339" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462061} :answer-field/id #uuid "a889bc2a-6c37-5857-b5df-2f84c3f8a657" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462784} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4072d32e-8787-592f-a6a0-ab69807057af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462063} {:answer/id #uuid "119a56a7-be8a-525d-bf38-85a10b27e983" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4072d32e-8787-592f-a6a0-ab69807057af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462063} :answer-field/id #uuid "115eacf4-2515-53aa-bfd6-ab8ce878fbab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462785} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac676307-c5cf-59c4-8590-312fc31f883c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462065} {:answer/id #uuid "298a07b4-50d6-5be9-96f1-5114af5fa7ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "298a07b4-50d6-5be9-96f1-5114af5fa7ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462066} :answer-field/id #uuid "99e4091b-8534-5001-a586-9ba94089c8a0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b1e210e-8810-5093-9deb-eb8812e9311b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122814" :question/problem "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 2.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-4$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=8,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨16{u}^{4}-12{u}^{2},\\,2u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false, while statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx={y}^{4}-3{y}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d69ae25e-4067-57d7-992a-aea277568ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462067} {:answer/id #uuid "738c6bee-a025-5815-b191-c51eede9211c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d69ae25e-4067-57d7-992a-aea277568ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462067} :answer-field/id #uuid "c61b6f96-e8f3-53f9-b0c0-da26da3e6072" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462787} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4efe198-1a08-51cc-bb7f-57e8f0ee8eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462069} {:answer/id #uuid "51e47506-7d0a-5b3e-b515-61f96ae37f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4efe198-1a08-51cc-bb7f-57e8f0ee8eb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462069} :answer-field/id #uuid "5edbd1d2-7f0f-56a6-b340-a1ec1e119077" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462788} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bba662d-b093-5629-b0a1-c818e13f06a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462071} {:answer/id #uuid "cad3636b-9235-5c64-8894-54bc8fd1a1b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cad3636b-9235-5c64-8894-54bc8fd1a1b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462072} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3bdd892-fdc2-556f-bf24-620230aff8e4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "533221ac-cdcc-53a5-adcd-03f57c6b1b57" :question/math-academy-id "q-122815" :question/problem "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(u)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{u}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{u}{2})⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2\\pi .$ \n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=2,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le \\pi .$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-1$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we note that both parameterizations traverse a half-circle of radius $1$ centered at $O$ between $0$ and $\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e05ec3e-cd64-5efe-b86c-3a85d32445a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462073} {:answer/id #uuid "555ded60-6e27-5822-bfad-111ae26de821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555ded60-6e27-5822-bfad-111ae26de821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462074} :answer-field/id #uuid "570b3d91-151c-5000-a5f6-67a9b778db1d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce53e294-37f1-5e16-892e-9c87da353bbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462075} {:answer/id #uuid "2fecce07-97ed-543c-9956-f750f8ecd7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce53e294-37f1-5e16-892e-9c87da353bbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462075} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c544999-5092-5e3f-ba7a-7f9b6e161fa2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462791} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d78c6e8e-5d8a-5dfc-b896-579c21a26b8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462077} {:answer/id #uuid "60092f97-7805-566d-a27b-a35ee30d9698" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d78c6e8e-5d8a-5dfc-b896-579c21a26b8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462077} :answer-field/id #uuid "6319433e-b1e6-54c4-9ece-69e71614667d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aba31fa9-c0e0-5ac2-bdfd-ad58b74f6f1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-122816" :question/problem "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{3/2}⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 4.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-3$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=12,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨4u,\\,8{u}^{3/2}⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3/2},\\,0\\le x\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "756cdc53-2932-5002-93f3-0e049675c868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462079} {:answer/id #uuid "c481b00c-7230-5985-9e66-4d8b6087f4e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "756cdc53-2932-5002-93f3-0e049675c868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462079} :answer-field/id #uuid "a52e79c6-6b76-598b-a0c0-137e3101dc68" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462793} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0be94117-938f-5e8d-b8dc-23f5959ac80d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462081} {:answer/id #uuid "d62869e1-04c3-5ef3-b5f6-f5bbc804f3f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0be94117-938f-5e8d-b8dc-23f5959ac80d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462081} :answer-field/id #uuid "da261af8-d4c1-56bf-8d02-1b93eb8f0515" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462794} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d76ae1f0-3cf0-5980-8be4-9864329b561e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462083} {:answer/id #uuid "668a58f5-744b-5464-a0b3-4a5197e2f210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "668a58f5-744b-5464-a0b3-4a5197e2f210" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462084} :answer-field/id #uuid "b55baf9c-63c9-5110-ad82-91c7b4d263f7" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462795}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "67eba06b-e142-51bc-86cf-6cd55545886d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122851" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+1},\\,3t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+1},\\,2u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{2k}{3}$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+1},\\,0\\le y\\le 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d626c071-0c70-52ac-bc79-16a2a3cf5cad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462085} {:answer/id #uuid "db1e1ca4-1a4a-5645-912d-ad584f2b5ce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db1e1ca4-1a4a-5645-912d-ad584f2b5ce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462086} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f97f6d4-1cc7-5a18-9002-6bc12e80f56c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8ec0988-8d3b-58bb-8f11-a31026537190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462087} {:answer/id #uuid "7122ea47-8dea-506b-a7e9-89375fe1971b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8ec0988-8d3b-58bb-8f11-a31026537190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462087} :answer-field/id #uuid "3eccce40-3459-5071-bdd9-96e4fe102f63" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462797} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd90f72-67c5-5198-8924-c359511557f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462089} {:answer/id #uuid "97613da4-4123-53e9-ac7f-e007a645737b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97613da4-4123-53e9-ac7f-e007a645737b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462090} :answer-field/id #uuid "56e9d11d-7777-5fe2-9ce3-8596ef406783" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "261c6852-f708-5ef6-9e89-3d88f4dbba8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122868" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨2t,\\,2\\sqrt{t}⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 2 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨4u,\\,2\\sqrt{2u}⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=2k$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{2x},\\,0\\le x\\le 4.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27cae781-a5b1-5d1a-a336-28677997d8d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521883} {:answer/id #uuid "43adf706-556a-5541-95dd-e56f093e98a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27cae781-a5b1-5d1a-a336-28677997d8d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521883} :answer-field/id #uuid "300668c7-94d5-5a1d-96ad-33fc31a43286" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4dc9fc-e868-51af-82a5-75a6f76b6034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521891} {:answer/id #uuid "5ba55c1e-3fc6-5f75-8886-bffde1bc1542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ba55c1e-3fc6-5f75-8886-bffde1bc1542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521898} :answer-field/id #uuid "3578c6fd-9b36-5337-acfe-ed0b376c2c06" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "833b8aa4-8f0f-54f8-bcd0-ad0222a4dce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521902} {:answer/id #uuid "afffdfaf-7ad9-5a48-8093-c75db5af7af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afffdfaf-7ad9-5a48-8093-c75db5af7af8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521911} :answer-field/id #uuid "74c7a9f5-1b9e-5e24-8415-8f6301839038" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1180df6e-fa40-51b3-98ac-1d4f6fae04df" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{25{t}^{2}+7},\\,5t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+7},\\,2u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{2k}{5}$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+7},\\,0\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ea6799-2d9f-5f37-95ae-72f2a5e9ca76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521879} {:answer/id #uuid "396d5a0c-09ce-5ae5-a8e9-bb9f1699e6cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09ea6799-2d9f-5f37-95ae-72f2a5e9ca76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521879} :answer-field/id #uuid "035d8c2d-9be7-5bbc-921f-3a6f151dc7d1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2370a66-c29c-5b37-89c6-2da05967bf6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521907} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d2de1b-0311-5bc7-9aee-5e7fbdce2a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2370a66-c29c-5b37-89c6-2da05967bf6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521907} :answer-field/id #uuid "34f3798f-9a31-575e-a080-fbc367dd1750" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3f12a61-204a-52df-a045-31308fbcfe09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521914} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5f2c45-a77f-5e71-a3fb-27da4adb38d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3f12a61-204a-52df-a045-31308fbcfe09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521914} :answer-field/id #uuid "367a4648-c48b-5ca7-beb6-0362f0f20418" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "44945cc2-d075-5615-b775-29cceef305cf" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨4t,\\,6\\sqrt{t}⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 5 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨20u,\\,6\\sqrt{5u}⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=5k$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{9x},\\,0\\le x\\le 20.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b68761-81ae-5727-8723-99155f456d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521896} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e75279-2f6c-585f-a49b-30410cd91345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b68761-81ae-5727-8723-99155f456d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521896} :answer-field/id #uuid "353ba0ff-733c-57e5-8e81-74317481335b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03178fdc-25eb-592a-aa45-4e266963dfb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521877} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cde8a0-0128-565a-a4cd-433dec39fb80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9cde8a0-0128-565a-a4cd-433dec39fb80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521925} :answer-field/id #uuid "84208a78-46f7-5cc8-aae2-ed3bf108cc3d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6080977b-5766-59b3-82b0-9891037d1857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521899} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c7ad3d-6caa-593c-b2d1-652348ed0ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5c7ad3d-6caa-593c-b2d1-652348ed0ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521922} :answer-field/id #uuid "a38cc838-6019-5577-98f0-f639569b05e7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8b2a59b4-567e-519b-bf4b-185eb8ce7675" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+6},\\,4t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨\\sqrt{25{u}^{2}+6},\\,5u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{5k}{4}$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+6},\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12383e44-707a-5bdc-aed6-bacd5d241604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521881} {:answer/id #uuid "d39317c7-f550-51db-95fa-14ecef4d8119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12383e44-707a-5bdc-aed6-bacd5d241604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521881} :answer-field/id #uuid "2849e85a-9324-5c9e-8606-379763c5280c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66fdd48e-d5d5-5dab-826a-ac4be0dd2146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521900} {:answer/id #uuid "f63ced98-a9ce-5a73-aa16-45250abe7b46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f63ced98-a9ce-5a73-aa16-45250abe7b46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521923} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b47340d-4902-5241-a3d9-513d7bd87af2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2c947ff-8de3-54d5-9100-bb93fe81f325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521921} {:answer/id #uuid "f7971d96-ca08-549f-84cc-5b72709d09cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7971d96-ca08-549f-84cc-5b72709d09cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521924} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd179a6-c2d5-5420-98bf-79fb4b48750e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7163cdf-b4ca-5487-945d-916df17c97fc" :question/problem "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨3{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 3.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-1$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨243{u}^{4}-18{u}^{2},\\,3u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement I is false, while statement III is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=3{y}^{4}-2{y}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a9f9a52-3082-5433-95a4-c5f4c8ae8cd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521897} {:answer/id #uuid "e91b5391-28fc-5690-8b2d-39d3a871a375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a9f9a52-3082-5433-95a4-c5f4c8ae8cd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521897} :answer-field/id #uuid "1993f2eb-5838-569b-889b-81d0a604df5e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3df0d4d-09b8-5201-b83b-666c7581491b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521909} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf41162-0ae6-5fde-a058-b41d64e5185f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbf41162-0ae6-5f